(No top-of-chart structure summary was given on this PDF — sections presented in the order they appear on the source chart: Verse 1, Pre-Chorus, Chorus, Interlude, Bridge 1, Bridge 2.)
(The "Yeshua" chorus line uses a heavily stretched, multi-line melisma notation in the original PDF that didn't extract cleanly — chord positions above are a best-effort reconstruction. Worth a visual double-check against the original PDF for that specific line. The two chorus passes differ slightly: the first ends with an extra F9/A chord the second doesn't have, so both are written in full rather than deduped. Bridge 2's second pass uses G5 instead of Gm on the first chord — written in full since the chords differ from the first pass.)
